Short:        Guest component for OS4 Test Bridge
Uploader:     ford@cathousestudio.com (fordprefect-amiga)
Author:       Cat House Studio
Type:         dev/cross
Version:      0.1.0
Architecture: ppc-amigaos
Requires:     AmigaOS 4.1 or later; shared transport directories between
              AmigaOS guest and Linux host; OS4 Test Bridge Linux host
              component required for bridge workflows. VS Code extension is
              optional and only required for VS Code integration.
Distribution: Aminet

OS4 Test Bridge is a development bridge between Linux and AmigaOS 4.
This archive contains the native AmigaOS 4 guest component used by that
workflow.

Archive contents:
- OS4TestBridge guest agent executable
- Payloads for bounded discovery/build/run operations
- Docs/INSTALL.txt, Docs/README.txt, Docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.txt
- S/startup-example

This archive is not a remote shell and does not provide arbitrary shell
execution. The bridge workflow uses typed, bounded operations and structured
request/result handling.

Validated reference environment:
- AmigaOS 4.1 on Sam460EX under QEMU/Kyvos
- GCC 11.5 target toolchain

Expected compatible:
- Other AmigaOS 4 environments with equivalent shared transport,
  process execution, and suitable SDK/toolchains

Not yet validated:
- All AmigaOS 4 hardware/emulator combinations

Installation:
1) Extract OS4TestBridge_OS4_0.1.0.lha on AmigaOS 4.
2) Start with Docs/INSTALL.txt.
3) See Docs/README.txt and Docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.txt.

Linux host component and VS Code integration are available from:
https://github.com/fordprefect-amiga/OS4TestBridge

GitHub release:
https://github.com/fordprefect-amiga/OS4TestBridge/releases/tag/v0.1.0
